a register-sized struct WITH a managed field ({n int; p @int}, 16 bytes: NeedsSret false but NeedsDestruction true) on a pointer-receiver method value from a call/temp is gated out of the 947 materialize fix — its by-value copy would need the managed field RefInc-d — so it stays the old dangling-pointer crash (reading m.n SIGSEGVs). Sibling of 948 (sret branch). Fix: sret-/refcount-aware struct-copy into the closure field. claude-todo.md.
